            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the suggestion!\n\nThe use case sounds like \"make it possible to jump to left/right side in next/prev direction\". If yes, then it is already possible as [`MiniAi.move_cursor()`](https://nvim-mini.org/mini.nvim/doc/mini-ai.html#miniai.move_cursor) allows specifying both side and direction (via `opts.search_method`). So something like this makes four mappings that would jump to either side of prev/next function call:\n\n```lua\nlocal map_jump = function(lhs, textobject_id, side, search_method)\n  local rhs = function()\n    MiniAi.move_cursor(side, 'a', textobject_id, { search_method = search_method, n_times = vim.v.count1 })\n  end\n  vim.keymap.set({ 'n', 'x', 'o' }, lhs, rhs)\nend\n\nmap_jump('[f', 'f', 'left', 'prev')\nmap_jump('[F', 'f', 'right', 'prev')\nmap_jump(']f', 'f', 'left', 'next')\nmap_jump(']F', 'f', 'right', 'next')\n```\n\nDoes this solve the original use case?",
