        {
            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": "I am sorry if my description wasn't clear enough. Mappings from your example: `[f`, `[F`, `]f`, `]F` is what I already use for jumping to a `f` textobject and it works great because there is an upper case variant of `f` which is `F`. The problem is that I also have symbol textobjects like textobject \\` which corresponds to a code sections in Markdown files. And this is what I get:  `[<symbol>`, `[<?>`, `]<symbol>`, `]<?>`(replace `<symbol>` with \\`). And I have nothing for `<?>` because there is no upper case variant of symbol \\`. So jumping to the next closest side of \\` textobject instead of being able to precisely choose which side exactly seems like the right fit for me.\n\nI did consider using a letter instead of a symbol for this textobject but unfortunately every letter in English alphabet is already taken for something else in my case ",
